Origin
  Archive: LZO_1-00.zip from the Hobbes OS/2 archive
  (https://www.hobbesgram.org/download/os2/dev-4/libraries-3/archivers/LZO_1-00.zip)
  sha256 142b4197d6ca3ed1fc7b031bcad344c7479f9e762e1dcf51f1c37a026a036890
  The author no longer publishes LZO 1.00 and no author-published checksum
  survives, so the hash above identifies the copy used, not its authenticity.
  Its contents are consistent with the release: GPL v2 COPYING, NEWS headed
  "Changes in 1.00 (13 Jul 1997)", LZO.lsm "Version: 1.00", lzoconf.h
  LZO_VERSION 0x1000 "Jul 13 1997".

What is here
  A subset of the release, files copied byte for byte with no edits:
    COPYING README AUTHORS NEWS LZO.lsm
    include/lzoconf.h include/lzo1x.h
    src/lzo1x_1.c src/lzo1x_d1.c src/config1x.h src/lzo_conf.h
    src/lzo_util.h src/lzo_dict.h src/lzo_ptr.h
    src/lzo1x_c.ch src/lzo1x_d.ch src/lzo1_d.ch
  Only the files these two sources include are kept; the rest of the
  release (other algorithms, minilzo, examples, build scripts) is omitted.

Modifications (gagarin, 2026)
  No source file is changed. The build configuration differs from the
  upstream defaults, set only by compiler flags in match/lib/lzo/lzo1x.c:
    /Gr /D__LZO_ENTRY=          public entry points use __fastcall
    /U_M_IX86                   no i386 unaligned-access paths
    /Dlzo_moff_t=lzo_ptrdiff_t  signed match offsets (selects the #else branch
    /Dlzo_cmoff_t=lzo_ptrdiff_t of the lzo_moff_t switch in src/lzo_conf.h)
  and match/lib/lzo/lzo1x.c compiles lzo1x_1.c and lzo1x_d1.c as one
  translation unit.
